---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---

<Base title="Privacy policy | EQLBRM LLC" description="How EQLBRM LLC handles information collected through this website.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="page-head">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">Last updated September 20, 2026.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="page-body legal">
      <p>
        This page explains what information {SITE.legalName} ("we") collects through eqlbrm.io, why we collect it, and
        how to reach us about it.
      </p>

      <h2>Information you send us</h2>
      <p>
        If you use the contact form, we receive your name, email address, and the message you write. We use it to reply
        to you. We don't sell it or share it for advertising. The form is delivered to us by an email service provider,
        which processes it on our behalf.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We use Google Tag Manager and Google Analytics to understand how people use this site, such as which pages are
        viewed, roughly where visitors are located, and what kind of device they use. These tools may set cookies in
        your browser. You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting and infrastructure</h2>
      <p>
        This site is hosted on Cloudflare, which may keep standard server logs (such as IP address and pages requested)
        for security and performance. Blog content is managed in Sanity, which does not receive information about
        visitors.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>
        This site links to services such as LinkedIn and Instagram. Their privacy practices are their own.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask us to see, correct, or delete the personal information we hold about you by emailing
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If we change this policy, we will update the date at the top of this page.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
